When writing or editing **user-facing text** (UI, errors, onboarding, marketing, help), follow `PRODUCT.md` → **Copy and punctuation**.

## Banned in user-facing strings

- Em dashes (—)
- En dashes (–) as punctuation or ranges
- Double hyphens (`--`) as dash substitutes

## Use instead

- Commas, colons, periods, or parentheses between ideas
- The word **to** for ranges (`13 to 120`, `3 to 4 oz`)
- **N/A** for missing numeric or time values (not `—`)

## Allowed

- Hyphens inside standard compound words (`USDA-backed`, `sign-in`, `If-then`, `Mifflin-St Jeor`)

## Before shipping copy

Search changed files for `—`, `–`, and ` -- ` in strings shown to users. Refactor before commit.
